{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgCFWVU6b2j3LBfYhjzxf", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I found the cause, but I can't fix it with the Honk tools, so I haven't proposed anything.\n\n**Cause:** The `mailer` pod is stuck in `CreateContainerConfigError`. The container `app` sets `securityContext.runAsNonRoot: true`, but its image (`busybox:1.36`) runs as root. The pod has no `runAsUser`, so the kubelet refuses to start it. The error is `container has runAsNonRoot and image will run as root`.\n\n**Why I haven't acted:** The Honk tools are `restart_pod`, `rollout_restart`, `scale` and `set_resources`. None of them can change a pod's security context. A restart or a scale would recreate the same pod with the same spec and fail the same way. Honk also reports no history for any of those actions on this problem.\n\n**Fix needed:** Someone with write access needs to change the Deployment spec in one of two ways:\n- **Preferred:** Add `runAsUser: 65534` (or any non-zero UID) to the container's `securityContext`. That keeps the non-root policy.\n- **Alternative:** Remove `runAsNonRoot: true`. That weakens the security policy.\n\nAfter the spec change, the Deployment will roll out a new pod on its own. I can check that it comes up Ready if you'd like."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 569, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25223, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 569}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "db72bb24-4a9e-400e-8202-0b7feccc788d", "uuid": "f39ce5c5-2369-4cfa-b2ad-5a0783d42874", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:46:45.111Z", "request_id": "req_011CgCFW